  "summary": "Malicious code in dolyame-boxy-atom-bnpl-store-button-set (npm)",
  "details": "On require, the package executes a multi-stage binary dropper. It fetches a second-stage payload over HTTPS from three Cloudflare Workers endpoints (oob-worker[.]cf99-9b3[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf101-adf[.]workers[.]dev, oob-worker[.]cf100-416[.]workers[.]dev) at path /pkg/package, with a DNS-TXT fallback channel via c[.]sdk[.]dl[.]wel1[.]ru and related *.dl[.]wel1[.]ru subdomains. The downloaded payload is written to /tmp/.cache_\u003chex\u003e (or dotnet_diag_\u003chex\u003e.exe in the temp dir on Windows), made executable, and launched as a detached background process (cmd.exe /c start /b on Windows, /bin/sh -c \"file \u0026\" on Unix). A stamp file (/tmp/.analytics_state) is used to run only once per session. The package also ships a large telemetry module that fingerprints the host (hostname, CPU count, memory, OS).",
